 "title": "Data Glitch",
 "category": "Effects",
 "text": "Sound: a stuttering burst of corrupted data: random pitches spraying out sixteen to the beat, crushed to a few bits.\n\nHow it's built: a Clock's 1/16 ticks a Sample & Hold whose random value goes into the oscillator's FM at two octaves (a new random pitch each tick) and retriggers a short envelope (a stutter per tick); the square goes through the Crusher (4 bits) and a Delay. One voice.\n\nPlay: hold a key.\n\nTweak: the clock's TEMPO, the oscillator's FM (how wild), BITS and RATE.",
